  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Summary",
      "html": "<p>Third-declension nouns show their stem in the genitive singular: ἐλπίς, ἐλπίδος (stem ἐλπιδ-); νύξ, νυκτός (stem νυκτ-); ἄρχων, ἄρχοντος (stem ἀρχοντ-). Learn every third-declension noun with its genitive and article. The endings are -ς, -ος, -ι, -α (or -ν) in the singular and -ες, -ων, -σι(ν), -ας in the plural. Before σ a dental drops (ἐλπίσι for ἐλπιδσι), a palatal and σ make ξ (νυξί), and ντ drops with the vowel lengthened (ἄρχουσι).</p>"
    },
